  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "7eb015747545051fb5e26ae2c6d5fa4c86e4de00",
      "message": "feat(runtime): retain verified release runtime evidence per launch (#5557)\n\n* feat(plan): sign and audit release runtime identity\n\n* feat(runtime): retain one verified release snapshot per selection\n\n* feat(runtime): thread verified sets through admission and custody\n\n* docs(security): record launch-scoped runtime proof limits\n\n* fix(runtime): preserve legacy fork admission with retained evidence\n\n* refactor(cli): reach runtime evidence through mvm-client\n\nThe check-thin-cli gate requires command code under crates/mvm-cli/src/commands\nto name no crate below mvm-client. The checkpoint fork boot reached\nmvm_runtime::runtime_evidence::verify_release_runtime_set directly, retaining\nlaunch-scoped verified release runtime evidence in a place the host library and\nSDKs cannot reach.\n\nRe-export verify_release_runtime_set (and its VerifiedRuntimeSet result type)\nfrom mvm-client's launch::runtime_source, next to the overlay and initramfs\nattach helpers it completes, and call it from the command through the existing\nmvm_client::launch::runtime_source re-export path. No behavior changes: the\nsame verification runs on the same fully assembled VmStartConfig.\n\n* chore: regenerate the process spawn inventory after the main merge\n\n* chore: satisfy the public-name and footprint gates for verified-runtime siblings\n\ncheck-public-function-names: the nine new f/f_with_verified_* sibling pairs are explained, not narrowed. Every base is pre-existing public API on main and is called from outside its defining scope, and the gate counts pub(crate) as public, so no visibility narrowing can remove a pair without deleting or privatizing shipped API. The _with_verified_* variants thread the launch-verified runtime set through admission and start so retained audit evidence matches what was actually verified; conflating the names would hide the verification boundary. Entries added to EXCEPTIONS with that justification.\n\ncheck-rust-footprint: raise the SLOC ceiling to 991178 and the physical-line ceiling to 1259462, the tree's honest measured totals after this change. The growth reflects the PR's verified-runtime launch-evidence retention work; the ratchet now pins the new totals."
    }
  ],
